6 Implementation focus and five-week timeline

The implementation focus should remain proportionate to the five-week prototype. The proposed
priorities are:
 1. correct the CDM datatype, requiredness and field-name inconsistencies, and make sure every

     collected field is either mapped or deliberately excluded;

 2. agree and implement the topic and record model, including narrative-first capture and times-
     tamped submissions;

 3. implement local authentication and server-side user-level access checks, and replace typed
     identifiers in file paths with server-generated ones;

 4. integrate and test the RDF mapping against the agreed field crosswalk;

 5. conduct functional testing and expert evaluation with Mirjam and Daniel.
    A local attachment demonstration using dummy files can be attempted if the core work is

stable. IPA SSO, production document storage, infrastructure-level encryption assurance and full
FDP registration remain future work because the required services and endpoints have not been
confirmed.

Figure 3: Proposed five-week SafeVoice implementation timeline. Task ownership and durations are
indicative and should be confirmed by the team.

