A.2 Reproducing selected findings

The following checks can be run from the repository root with the repository’s own code. Each
check needs only Python, pandas and PyYAML. The AllegroGraph connection is not needed.

• W1-01: call create_cdm_column_map from cleaner.py on the CDM file. All returned datatype
    values are None.

• W1-03 and W1-05: flatten a payload shaped like the one in app.py with pandas.json_norm
    alize (separator _) and compare the column names with the $(...) placeholders in the YAML
    mapping. Only data_victim_count has no matching column, and five collected columns are
    never used.

• W1-06: open the form without touching any field, or run app.py with Streamlit’s AppTest,
    and read the widget values. Coordinates are 0.0 and the drop-downs show their first option.

• W3-04: call save_triples_to_file from mapper.py with the filename ../../test_batch.nt.
    The file is written to the repository root instead of data/intermediate.

B Limitations

This report analyses the public repository branch inspected on 4 November 2026. The team’s local
working copy may contain changes that are not present in that branch. The report does not claim
that infrastructure-level controls are absent merely because they are not implemented in application
code. In particular, disk encryption, backup protection, server permissions, organisational SSO and
IPA document storage require confirmation from the relevant infrastructure owners. The default
values described in W1-06 depend on the Streamlit version and on the content of the drop-down file.
The final CDM fields and RDF predicates should be reviewed with Mirjam and Daniel. Synthetic
or properly anonymised data should be used for development and demonstrations.

